---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import PlanningCTA from '../components/PlanningCTA.astro';
import { images } from '../data/assets';
const breadcrumbs=[{label:'Join a Trip',href:'/join-a-trip/'}];
const formats=[
  {title:'Active & Trekking Departures',image:images.trekking,copy:'Selected hiking, mountain, and active journeys that can work for individual travelers or smaller groups joining a shared departure.',tags:['Active','Trekking','Small group']},
  {title:'Learn-To Departures',image:images.surf,copy:'Skill-led trips built around learning, progression, and destination time, with specific prerequisites explained before booking.',tags:['Beginner-friendly','Skill-based','Instruction']},
  {title:'Culture, Coast & Cruise',image:images.coast,copy:'Hosted or coordinated journeys with more emphasis on culture, social travel, comfort, and selected active experiences.',tags:['Culture','Hosted','Comfort-forward']}
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Join a Trip | Upcoming Talon Expeditions Departures" description="Learn how selected Talon Expeditions hosted and small-group departures are released, including active, learn-to, cultural, cruise, and experience-led travel." image={images.coast} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}>
  <section class="page-hero" style={`background-image:url('${images.coast}')`}><div class="shell"><Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs}/><p class="eyebrow">Join a Talon trip</p><h1 class="section-title">Selected departures for travelers who do not need to bring the whole group.</h1><p>Private groups are the center of Talon Expeditions, but selected hosted or small-group departures can open specific trip concepts to individual travelers. Each public departure is published only when the itinerary, supplier structure, dates, participant requirements, and booking terms are ready to explain clearly.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="answer-panel"><h2>Are there public Talon Expeditions departures available now?</h2><p>Talon Expeditions uses a selective departure model rather than a high-volume catalog. This page is the permanent home for joinable trips, and each published departure includes dates, destination, pricing, inclusions, activity level, booking terms, and participant requirements so travelers can evaluate the trip before inquiring.</p></div><div class="specialty-heading" style="margin-top:52px"><div><p class="eyebrow">Trip formats</p><h2 class="section-title">The kinds of departures that fit the Talon model.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">Public departures are built around clear trip concepts and released when the operational details are ready. Private groups can use the same formats on their own dates without waiting for a scheduled departure.</p></div><div class="destination-grid">{formats.map((item)=><div class="destination-card" style={`background-image:url('${item.image}')`}><div class="destination-content"><span class="tagline">Selected departure format</span><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.copy}</p><div class="mini-tags">{item.tags.map((tag)=><span>{tag}</span>)}</div></div></div>)}</div></div></section>
  <section class="section soft-section"><div class="shell"><div class="specialty-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">How public departures work</p><h2 class="section-title">A real trip page should answer the questions before asking for a deposit.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">Each published departure is designed as a complete trip page with enough operational detail to make an informed decision.</p></div><div class="why-grid"><div class="why-item"><span class="number">01</span><h3>Dates & meeting point</h3><p>Exact travel dates, start/end locations, and arrival expectations.</p></div><div class="why-item"><span class="number">02</span><h3>Daily experience</h3><p>Route, activities, accommodation, pacing, free time, and what changes by day.</p></div><div class="why-item"><span class="number">03</span><h3>Price & inclusions</h3><p>What is included, likely extras, single-room assumptions, air model, and payment milestones.</p></div><div class="why-item"><span class="number">04</span><h3>Readiness & terms</h3><p>Fitness, skills, equipment, documents, insurance, minimum group, and cancellation conditions.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section dark-section"><div class="shell contact-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Departure list</p><h2 class="section-title">Hear when a real departure opens.</h2><p style="color:#aaa">Tell us which trip styles interest you. We will use that information to understand demand and contact you when an appropriate public departure is ready. This is an interest list, not a booking.</p></div><form data-mailto-form data-subject="Talon Expeditions departure interest" class="form-panel contact-form" action="mailto:sales@talonexpeditions.com" method="post" enctype="text/plain" style="color:var(--ink)"><div><label for="join-name">Name</label><input id="join-name" name="name" required/></div><div><label for="join-email">Email</label><input id="join-email" type="email" name="email" required/></div><div><label for="join-style">Trip style</label><select id="join-style" name="trip-style"><option>Active / trekking</option><option>Learn-to / skill based</option><option>Culture / cruise</option><option>Wildlife / nature</option><option>Open to several styles</option></select></div><div><label for="join-region">Home region</label><input id="join-region" name="home-region" placeholder="City / state / country"/></div><div class="full"><label for="join-note">What would make you join a trip?</label><textarea id="join-note" name="note" placeholder="Destinations, activity level, time of year, budget range, or anything else useful."></textarea></div><div class="full"><button class="button" type="submit">Join the Interest List</button><p class="form-note">You can also send departure interests directly to sales@talonexpeditions.com.</p></div></form></div></section>
  <PlanningCTA title="Already have your own group? You do not need to wait for a public departure." copy="Private groups can start planning around their own dates, interests, activity level, and travel style." />
</BaseLayout>
